        "original_id": "aeab1fb0-a052-583d-b6be-8d6b4432973f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Groups: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Places: Japan\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946.\n- Benny Andersson is a Swedish musician and composer.\n- Benny Andersson was a member of the Swedish music group ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- ABBA recorded the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" was released as a single the year after its original release with \"Money, Money, Money\" as the B-side.\n- In Japan, the single \"That's Me\" was released to promote ABBA's album \"Arrival\".\n- In Japan, the single \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "97324f87-69ae-5916-97af-1e8c8c35c97b",
        "text": "Page: Money, Money, Money. Sentence: \"Money, Money, Money\" is a song recorded by Swedish pop group ABBA, written by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus.\nPage: Benny Andersson. Sentence: Göran Bror Benny Andersson (] ; born 16 December 1946) is a Swedish musician, composer, member of the Swedish music group ABBA (1972–1982), and co-composer of the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\nPage: That's Me. Sentence: It was released as a single in Japan the following year (with \"Money, Money, Money\" as the B-side) to promote the band's \"Arrival\" album, and reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
